<title>LATVIA: STATE SECTOR WAGES UP 2.3 PCT IN FEB.</title>
<headline>STATE SECTOR WAGES UP 2.3 PCT IN FEB.</headline>
<dateline>RIGA 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Latvia's statistics committee said on Wednesday that salaries in the state and municipal sector increased in February by 2.3 percent versus January while consumer prices rose by 0.4 percent.</p>
<p>Gross average salaries in the state and municipal sector in February 1997 were 120 lats versus 117 lats in January, the committee said in a statement.</p>
<p>Net salaries in February were 88.42 lats or 73.5 percent of the gross sum.</p>
<p>&quot;The changes in salaries were influenced by the increase of social tax from five to nine percent,&quot; the statement said.</p>
<p>-- Riga Newsroom, +371 721 5240</p>
